Total	29	


Run from the order-service directory with Java 21 and Docker available:
./mvnw clean verify
On Windows PowerShell, use ./mvnw.cmd clean verify instead.
Verified Email Example
For order #3, the inbox received:
Email subject	Observed result
Order Received	Order #3 received, initial status PENDING
Payment FAILED	Order #3 payment outcome reported as FAILED


This verifies the email delivery path for an order-received event and a failed-payment event. Payment-success notifications were also generated by the application during earlier testing, but a successful-payment email delivery is not separately claimed here.
During testing, CloudWatch also helped identify an SES sandbox rejection for an unverified recipient. Using a verified recipient resolved the issue without changing application code.
API Overview
All requests should go through the API Gateway.
Local base URL: http://localhost:8765
Users
POST /api/users/register
POST /api/users/login
GET  /api/users/getUser
Orders
POST  /api/orders
GET   /api/orders
GET   /api/orders/{orderId}
PATCH /api/orders/{orderId}/status
POST  /api/orders/{orderId}/cancel
Payments
POST  /api/payments
GET   /api/payments/{paymentId}
GET   /api/payments/order/{orderId}
PATCH /api/payments/{paymentId}/status
Notifications
POST /api/notifications
GET  /api/notifications
GET  /api/notifications/{notificationId}
POST /api/notifications/{notificationId}/mark-as-read
POST /api/notifications/mark-all-as-read
Sample Registration
POST http://localhost:8765/api/users/register
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "username": "maggie",
  "email": "maggie@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}
Sample Login
POST http://localhost:8765/api/users/login
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "email": "maggie@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}
Use the returned JWT for protected endpoints:
Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>
Sample Order Creation
POST http://localhost:8765/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "customerName": "Maggie Lorena",
  "customerEmail": "maggie@example.com",
  "customerPhone": "6145551001",
  "items": [
    {
      "productName": "Laptop Stand",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 59.99
    },
    {
      "productName": "Wireless Keyboard",
      "quantity": 1,
      "price": 79.99
    }
  ]
}
The order initially has status PENDING, then becomes CONFIRMED or PAYMENT_FAILED after asynchronous payment processing.
Email testing: The customerEmail value in the order event determines the recipient of order and payment emails. Logging in with an email address does not automatically change this field. While SES is in sandbox mode, use a verified recipient address for testing.
Run Locally with Docker Compose
Prerequisites
- Docker and Docker Compose
- Environment-specific configuration and credentials for databases, RabbitMQ, JWT, and email where required
  From the project root:
docker compose build --no-cache
docker compose up -d
Check containers:
docker compose ps
View logs:
docker compose logs -f
Stop the stack:
docker compose down
