The business services use Spring Boot's layered structure, including controllers, services, repositories, entities, DTOs, configuration, and RabbitMQ publishers/consumers where applicable.
Engineering Highlights
- Designed independently deployable microservices with distinct business responsibilities.
- Secured API access with Spring Security and JWT-based authentication.
- Implemented event-driven workflows using RabbitMQ to decouple order creation, payment processing, and notifications.
- Used independent relational databases for service data ownership.
- Built Docker-based local development and AWS ECS Fargate deployment workflows.
- Automated image builds, ECR pushes, and ECS updates using GitHub Actions and OIDC.
- Integrated AWS SES SMTP for transactional emails and diagnosed delivery failures using CloudWatch logs.
- Verified the deployed workflow end to end, including actual customer email delivery.
Future Improvements
- Extend automated tests to other services and add a dedicated cross-service end-to-end test in CI.
- Stable HTTPS API endpoint using a load balancer and custom domain.
- Production-ready secret management and least-privilege access reviews.
- RabbitMQ retries, dead-letter queues, and idempotent event consumers.
- Reliable email retries and delivery/bounce monitoring.
- Distributed tracing, metrics, and alerting.
- OpenAPI/Swagger documentation.
- Refresh tokens, logout, and fine-grained role-based authorization.
- Real payment provider integration and secure payment retry workflows.
- AWS SES production access for sending to unverified customer addresses.
